+\section*{Correction notice (v1.3)}
+\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Correction notice (v1.3)}
+\noindent\textbf{What this version corrects.} This version \emph{withdraws a
+claim}. Through v1.2, \S\ref{sec:disc} stated that the present paper
+\emph{completes part (ii)(a) for $d=2$} of the master conjecture
+of~\cite{Sakai}. Part (ii)(a) of~\cite{Sakai} concerns the Edge--Borel
+coefficient, a different object from the connection coefficient $C$ studied
+here; \cite{Sakai} records the distinction in its Observation on p.~4. The
+sentence is replaced by one that states what Theorem~\ref{thm:main}
+establishes and records part (ii)(a) as open. This is a withdrawal, not an
+additive clarification.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Surface type.} The previous version described $\C$ as ``the
+rank-one standalone closure on the Sakai surface $D_5^{(1)}$ (Painlev\'e~V)''
+without qualification. That classification is Conjecture~4.1 of the companion
+paper~\cite{Vquad} (\texttt{10.5281/zenodo.20455089}, read at v1.2), and this
+version carries it as conjectural throughout.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Build script.} The bundled \texttt{build.py} carried a
+reproducibility target naming the v1.0 PDF, which it retained through v1.2. A
+reproduction run therefore compared a freshly built PDF against superseded
+bytes. The target now names this version's PDF.
+
+\noindent\textbf{What is unchanged.} Theorem~\ref{thm:main} and its proof; the
+$46$-digit agreement of the three independent verifications; every numerical
+value; the differential-Galois and resurgence results; and the conditional
+transcendence statement. No computation is affected.
+
+\noindent\textbf{Sequencing.} The same correction will be carried into the
+journal manuscript at revision. A reader who arrives at this record from the
+manuscript's data-availability statement may therefore find, until that
+revision appears, a manuscript whose corresponding sentences have not yet been
+corrected; this record is the corrected text.
+
